---
// src/pages/support.astro
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Support"
  description="Get help with PatreonTV — FAQ, common issues, and contact."
>
  <h1>Support</h1>
  <p>
    PatreonTV is early-stage and open-source. If you hit something
    unexpected, we'd like to hear about it.
  </p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <h3>How do I sign in?</h3>
  <p>
    On first launch, PatreonTV asks for your Patreon <code>session_id</code>
    cookie. On a computer, sign in at patreon.com, open the browser's
    developer tools (Application → Cookies in Chrome, or Storage → Cookies
    in Firefox/Safari), copy the value of the <code>session_id</code>
    cookie, and paste it into the TV using the Apple TV Remote keyboard on
    your iPhone or iPad.
  </p>

  <h3>Why can't I see a post I know I paid for?</h3>
  <p>
    Make sure you signed in with the same Patreon account that has the
    membership. If a specific post still doesn't appear, try
    force-quitting and reopening the app, or sign out and paste a fresh
    <code>session_id</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>A video won't play. What now?</h3>
  <p>
    Try these in order:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Sign out and back in from <strong>Settings → Sign Out</strong>.</li>
    <li>
      If the post uses a YouTube or Vimeo embed, PatreonTV can't play it
      in-app — you'll see a "Watch on…" prompt to open the original service.
    </li>
    <li>
      If the video is Patreon-hosted and still fails, please contact us
      (below) with the post title and creator name so we can investigate.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Is my Patreon password stored on your servers?</h3>
  <p>
    No. You sign in on Patreon's own website — your password is never
    seen by our code. You copy the session cookie Patreon issued and
    paste it directly into the Apple TV, where it is stored only in the
    tvOS Keychain. No intermediary server receives it. See our
    <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h3>Does watching in PatreonTV support the creator?</h3>
  <p>
    You continue to support the creator through your existing Patreon
    membership — PatreonTV doesn't change that in either direction. To
    upgrade a tier or start a new membership, visit patreon.com or the
    official Patreon app.
  </p>

  <h3>Can I use PatreonTV without an Apple TV?</h3>
  <p>
    PatreonTV is Apple TV only. There is no iPhone, iPad, Mac, Android,
    Fire TV, or Roku version.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting an issue</h2>
  <p>
    We track bugs and feature requests on GitHub. If you're comfortable
    filing there:
    <a
      href="https://github.com/DevelopmentCats/patreon-tv/issues"
      rel="noopener">github.com/DevelopmentCats/patreon-tv/issues</a>.
    Include your Apple TV model, tvOS version, and steps to reproduce.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For anything not covered above — including privacy or security
    concerns — open an issue on
    <a
      href="https://github.com/DevelopmentCats/patreon-tv/issues"
      rel="noopener">GitHub</a>. For security reports, please use
    <a
      href="https://github.com/DevelopmentCats/patreon-tv/security/advisories/new"
      rel="noopener">GitHub's private vulnerability reporting</a>
    instead of a public issue. We aim to reply within a few business days.
  </p>
</Base>
